# Fork-specific commit scopes for the Go rewrite (one per line; # = comment).
#
# The scoped-commits gate also accepts automatically: every spec/feature `id:`
# in specs/ & features/, the `specs` scope, each features/<slug>, the harness
# areas (hooks, skills, commands, agents, templates, rules, docs, mise, readme),
# and `treewide`. Declare here only what isn't derivable that way — the Go
# package areas under internal/ and cmd/, plus fork meta-scopes.

# Go implementation areas
cli            # cmd/specify
project        # internal/project — init + per-agent projection
engine         # internal/engine — scan/verify/drift/cover/parity/gate/lock/ledger
specmodel      # internal/specmodel — the spec model parser
coreassets     # internal/coreassets — embedded prompts/templates
config         # internal/config — .speckit/specs.json (targets, deploy manifest)
scaffold       # internal/scaffold — stack scaffold + .github/deploy renderer
github         # internal/github — REST+GraphQL client (Issues/Projects/secrets/rulesets)
reports        # internal/reports — junit/xunit/event-stream adapters
integrations   # internal/integrations
extensions     # internal/extensions

# Repo infrastructure
ci             # .github/ workflows + the hosted gate action/reusable workflow

# Fork meta
fork           # fork establishment, provenance, FORK.md
spike          # throwaway spikes/
